The management has approved an information security policy, and the people in the organisation know it.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs an ISMS. NIS2 requires policies on risk analysis and information system security from essential and important entities.

== How to implement

Write the information security policy, with the high-level objectives and the commitments, and get the approval of the management. Write the cryptography rules, based on the ECCG Agreed Cryptographic Mechanisms (ACM), and get them approved. List the topic-specific policies in the policy. They can be other documents in the process register, for example for access control or for the use of cloud services. The policy has an objective for the use of AI, and the AI policy is in the table of topic-specific policies. The AI policy is evidence of the control "Set the AI policy" of the AI use basics library. Communicate the policy to the employees and to the relevant contractors, and record their confirmations.

